    "The newly priced b uses exact rational moment engines and a10^-16 bad-class fallback; it is not a new Lean theorem at that exponent.",
    "Byte regeneration certifies data provenance, not proof execution. The integration remains a conditional finite construction.",
    "Upstream whole-block WHT/Fourier claims do not formalize the bit side, integer multiplication, analytic routing interfaces, or the new corrected physical guard.",
    "Lean does not read the total-frame field according to upstream mutation evidence; Python frame/scalar/lifetime/physical checks remain mandatory."
